{%- comment -%}
  One of Walter's two hand-drawn frames, with content sitting inside its opening.

  The frames are photographs of ink on paper: transparent inside the opening AND outside the
  drawing, so a frame can sit over anything. That also means the opening is not a CSS box — it is
  a hole in a picture — and the only way to put content in it is to position the content against
  measured insets.

  Measured off the source PNGs on 9 Oct 2026 by walking out from the centre of the alpha channel
  to the first opaque pixel:

    rect     2000 × 3200   opening inset  L 11.75%  R 12.20%  T 7.72%   B 8.94%
    scallop  2934 × 4698   opening inset  L 17.35%  R 15.71%  T 11.22%  B 11.24%

  The frame is never stretched: its own aspect ratio is held by `aspect-ratio` on the wrapper, and
  the picture fills it exactly. Change the width, the height follows. If content needs more room
  than the opening gives, the content scrolls or shrinks — the frame does not.

  Both widths and heights are set on the <img> so nothing shifts while it loads.

  Accepts:
    shape   'rect' (default) or 'scallop'
    width   600 | 900 | 1400  — the asset to load (default 900)
    class   extra classes on the wrapper
    content the markup to place inside the opening (use a capture)

  Usage:
    {%- capture inner -%}<p>…</p>{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- render 'wui-frame', shape: 'rect', width: 900, content: inner -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign f_shape = shape | default: 'rect'
  assign f_width = width | default: 900

  if f_shape == 'scallop'
    assign f_ratio = '2934 / 4698'
    assign f_native_h = 1441
  else
    assign f_ratio = '2000 / 3200'
    assign f_native_h = 1440
  endif

  case f_width
    when 600
      assign f_h = f_native_h | times: 600 | divided_by: 900
    when 1400
      assign f_h = f_native_h | times: 1400 | divided_by: 900
    else
      assign f_width = 900
      assign f_h = f_native_h
  endcase

  assign png = 'wui-frame-' | append: f_shape | append: '-' | append: f_width | append: '.png'
  assign webp = 'wui-frame-' | append: f_shape | append: '-' | append: f_width | append: '.webp'
-%}
<div class="wui-frame wui-frame--{{ f_shape }} {{ class }}" style="aspect-ratio: {{ f_ratio }};">
  <picture>
    <source srcset="{{ webp | asset_url }}" type="image/webp">
    <img
      class="wui-frame__edge"
      src="{{ png | asset_url }}"
      width="{{ f_width }}"
      height="{{ f_h }}"
      alt=""
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
    >
  </picture>
  <div class="wui-frame__opening">{{ content }}</div>
</div>
